---
title: Boiled Eggs
servings: 1
yields: 1
tags:
  - entres
source:
  name: Serious Eats
  url: https://www.seriouseats.com/the-secrets-to-peeling-hard-boiled-eggs
-- introduction: 
---

Bring a pot of water to boil that has enough water to handle however many eggs you are going to boil (don't want cold eggs dropping the water temperature too much).

Lower @egg{1} into the boiling water gently and continue boiling for 30 seconds.

Reduce heat to a low simmer and let cook for an additional ~{8%minutes}.\
> for **your** preferred eggs, use [this](https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/ca7nmQUsd3_JfMCOhLUQ183hiXY=/750x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc():format(webp)/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__images__2014__05__09242009-egg-boiling-timing-32136fe3344a4899ab9b3ae49e72f0eb.jpg) as a cook time reference.

While you are waiting for the eggs to cook, make an ice bath.

Immediately once the eggs are done, submerge them in the ice bath until completely cooled.

Peel and enjoy.